 "title": "Неожиданный поворот  (An Unexpected Turn)",
 "level": "A1 — Duolingo Section 2",
 "labels": {
  "kostya": "Костя",
  "nastya": "Настя"
 },
 "segments": [
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "The serious talk between Nastya and Kostya goes on. Nastya is quite sure what she wants, and Kostya is struggling to keep up. We'll hear it in Russian first.",
   "gap": 0.8
  },
  {
   "v": "kostya",
   "t": "Ты сейчас серьёзно?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "nastya",
   "t": "Да, я абсолютно серьёзна.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "kostya",
   "t": "Я этого не ожидал.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "nastya",
   "t": "Тебе следовало этого ожидать.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "kostya",
   "t": "Вчера всё было так хорошо.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "nastya",
   "t": "Вчера осталось в прошлом.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "kostya",
   "t": "Что ты хочешь от меня?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "nastya",
   "t": "Я хочу серьёзных отношений.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "kostya",
   "t": "Я очень стараюсь.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "nastya",
   "t": "Этого недостаточно, Костя.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "kostya",
   "t": "Ты на меня сердишься?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "nastya",
   "t": "Нет, я не сержусь.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "kostya",
   "t": "Ты не счастлива со мной?",
   "gap": 0.9
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "Let's replay it step by step.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "kostya",
   "t": "Ты сейчас серьёзно?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Are you serious right now?' There's no verb, just 'you now seriously'. 'Seriously' ends in 'o', like many words that say how.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "nastya",
   "t": "Да, я абсолютно серьёзна.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Yes, I'm completely serious.' 'Serious' has an 'a' at the end because Nastya is a woman. 'Completely' is a borrowed word.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "kostya",
   "t": "Я этого не ожидал.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'I didn't expect this.' After a negative, 'this' takes the 'of' form, 'etogo'. 'Expected' ends in the masculine 'l'.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "nastya",
   "t": "Тебе следовало этого ожидать.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'You should have expected it.' The word 'sledovalo' is neuter and means 'it was due', from 'follow'. 'To you' is the first word.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "kostya",
   "t": "Вчера всё было так хорошо.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Everything was so good yesterday.' 'Was' is neuter, to go with 'everything'. 'So good' is two small words.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "nastya",
   "t": "Вчера осталось в прошлом.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Yesterday is in the past.' The line really says 'yesterday stayed in the past'. 'In the past' ends in 'om'.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "kostya",
   "t": "Что ты хочешь от меня?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'What do you want from me?' 'You want' is irregular, ending in 'sh'. 'From me' is a small word and 'menya'.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "nastya",
   "t": "Я хочу серьёзных отношений.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'I want a serious relationship.' After 'want', the plural takes the 'of' form. So 'serious' and 'relationships' both change.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "kostya",
   "t": "Я очень стараюсь.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'I'm trying my best.' 'Try' ends in 'sya'. 'Very' sits in front of it.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "nastya",
   "t": "Этого недостаточно, Костя.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'It's not enough, Kostya.' The word is built from 'not' plus 'enough'. 'This' takes the 'of' form.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "kostya",
   "t": "Ты на меня сердишься?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Are you angry with me?' Russians are angry 'on' someone. 'Be angry' ends in 'sya'.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "nastya",
   "t": "Нет, я не сержусь.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'No, I'm not angry.' The 'd' of 'angry' changes to 'zh' for 'I'. It is the same change as in 'I see'.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "kostya",
   "t": "Ты не счастлива со мной?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Aren't you happy with me?' 'Happy' ends in 'a' for a woman. 'With me' is the irregular 'so mnoy'. Now let's listen to the whole conversation again from start to finish.",
   "gap": 0.9
  },
  {
   "v": "kostya",
   "t": "Ты сейчас серьёзно?",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "v": "nastya",
